Done. `src/dispatcher.js` now computes backoff as `Math.floor(random() * Math.min(baseDelayMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1), jitterCapMs))`, drawing exactly once per wait. The existing `jitter` option remains as an alias for the same source, so current tests still pass; `maxAttempts: 1` still sleeps zero times. Added a capped-schedule test verifying `[50, 75, 75]`, one draw per wait, and no delay above the cap — `node --test` passes 66/66.
